# ── Python environment ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DisloClusterVenv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Third-party libraries kept beside the repository ─────────────────────────
# SUNDIALS for the 0-D solver, and the private Eigen 3.4.0 that
# Docs/Formulation/build_modelib.sh fetches when the system has only Eigen 5.
# Sources, not artifacts of this project: reproducible from the build script.
Libraries/

# ── Build trees ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ZrMicro/build/
MoDELib3/build/
MoDELib3/build_dc/
# Any additional MoDELib build tree, e.g. build_fast/ for the optimized
# fast solve alongside build_dc/ as the reference. Same rule as above:
# regenerable, and a committed Linux ELF once made a clone believe
# MoDELib was built when it was not.
MoDELib3/build_*/
ZrMicro/.vscode/c_cpp_properties.json

# ── Run output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Run directories are large and fully reproducible from the config.json each
# one carries, so only the directory's README is tracked.
Simulations/output/*
!Simulations/output/README.md
# Runs made before Simulations/output/ existed. ZrMicro moved to the repository
# root, so this path lost its ZrClusterDynamics/ prefix -- leaving the old one
# in place silently un-ignored 1.4 GB of run output.
ZrMicro/output/

# Staged MoDELib cases, which `driver.prepare` generates and names
# <type>_<size>nm_o<order>_<domain-key> (plus a _qssa twin for the fast solve).
# They hold the mesh, the inputFiles and multi-MB evl blocks -- 152 MB for two
# domains -- and are fully reproducible from the domain.json each one carries,
# so they belong with the run output rather than in git. The hand-authored
# reference cases (zrmicro_coupled, zr3d_500nm, irradiation_*) do not match
# this pattern and stay tracked.
MoDELib3/tutorials/cubic_*nm_o[12]_*/
MoDELib3/tutorials/hexagonal_*nm_o[12]_*/

# ── Editor / OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# ── Cowork cleanup staging ──
_to_delete/

# Hardening DD cases staged by dislocluster_code.studies.hardening: same rule as
# the coupled cases above -- mesh, inputFiles and multi-MB evl/F output, all
# reproducible from the hardening.json each one carries. No trailing slash: a
# `campaign` run leaves its `<tag>_campaign.json` result file BESIDE the case
# directories, and that is output too.
MoDELib3/tutorials/hardening_*

# Office lock/owner files: Word, Excel and PowerPoint write a `~$<name>` stub
# beside an open document and remove it on close. One was committed with the
# hardening work (`~$RFQ-2185_Kickoff.pptx`, 165 bytes).
~$*

# latexmk's own bookkeeping. Both record ABSOLUTE paths of every input file
# (`d:/GitHub/DisloCluster/...`), so they churn between machines and between
# checkouts the way a CMake cache does. The .aux/.log/.out/.toc that this repo
# does track are path-free and reproducible; these two are not.
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk

# latexmk console capture (see the .log the engine writes itself).
build.log

# Figure build intermediates and material-file backups are products, not sources.
Docs/Formulation/self-consistent/SC_manuscript/figures/_loops_all_panels/
MoDELib3/Library/Materials/*.bak_*
